</table>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2 </span>Models</h3>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S3.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 3.2 Models ‣ 3 Datasets, Models, Prompt Design and Metrics ‣ Enhancing the Learning Experience: Using Vision-Language Models to Generate Questions for Educational Videos" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> shows the selected models and the characteristics of their input modalities.
Each VLM uses one of two main approaches to frame processing:</p>
<span id="S3.I1" class="ltx_inline-enumerate">
<span id="S3.I1.i1" class="ltx_inline-item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_inline-item">1.</span> <em id="S3.I1.i1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Selective frame usage: </em><span id="S3.I1.i1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Video-LLaVA</span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">29</a>]</cite><span id="S3.I1.i1.4" class="ltx_text">,
</span></span>
<span id="S3.I1.i2" class="ltx_inline-item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_inline-item">2.</span> <em id="S3.I1.i2.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Comprehensive frame sampling: </em><span id="S3.I1.i2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">PG-Video-LLaVA</span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">38</a>]</cite><span id="S3.I1.i2.4" class="ltx_text">, <span id="S3.I1.i2.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Video-LLaMA</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">54</a>]</cite>
</span></span>
</span>
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Additionally, we include the instruction-tuned version of the LLM <span id="S3.SS2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Mistral-7B</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>]</cite> to pair with the VLM model variants since LLMs have already been used for question generation in previous research <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>]</cite>.
This model takes a prompt and the transcript as input for processing.
Notably, <span id="S3.SS2.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Video-LLaMA</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">54</a>]</cite> processes the original audio signal, while <span id="S3.SS2.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">PG-Video-LLaVA</span> transcribes speech.
We use a zero-shot approach of the monomodal models <span id="S3.SS2.p1.2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Video-LLaVA</span> and <span id="S3.SS2.p1.2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Mistral-7B</span> as a baseline to assess the extent to which multimodal models perform.
All models use prompts, allowing analysis of how prompt formulation affects results.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 3: </span>Selected models and their characteristics for automatic question generation. <span id="S3.T3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">All</span> for <span id="S3.T3.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">#Frames</span> frames extraction at a regular interval. <span id="S3.T3.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Audio</span> describes the use of the original audio signal present, whereas text represents the use of speech transcript.</figcaption>
