<td id="S4.T4.22.16.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right">89.83 %</td>
<td id="S4.T4.22.16.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right">10.17 %</td>
<td id="S4.T4.22.16.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_r"><span id="S4.T4.22.16.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.00 %</span></td>
<td id="S4.T4.22.16.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.12</td>
<td id="S4.T4.22.16.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.02</td>
<td id="S4.T4.22.16.8" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.04</td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T4.22.17" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T4.22.17.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">Video-LLaMA</td>
<td id="S4.T4.22.17.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">Avg.</td>
<td id="S4.T4.22.17.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb">87.98 %</td>
<td id="S4.T4.22.17.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb">12.02 %</td>
<td id="S4.T4.22.17.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb ltx_border_r"><span id="S4.T4.22.17.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.00 %</span></td>
<td id="S4.T4.22.17.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">0.12</td>
<td id="S4.T4.22.17.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">0.01</td>
<td id="S4.T4.22.17.8" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">0.04</td></tr>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The zero-shot evaluation of <span id="S4.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Mistral-7B</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>]</cite> and <span id="S4.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Video-LLaVA</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">29</a>]</cite> serves as a baseline comparison for multimodal VLMs.
The performance of the multimodal VLMs is assessed at both the zero-shot and fine-tuned levels (Section <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 Fine-Tuning Setting ‣ 4 Comparing VLMs for Video Question Generation ‣ Enhancing the Learning Experience: Using Vision-Language Models to Generate Questions for Educational Videos" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>).
Table <a href="#S4.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ 4.1 Zero-Shot Setting ‣ 4 Comparing VLMs for Video Question Generation ‣ Enhancing the Learning Experience: Using Vision-Language Models to Generate Questions for Educational Videos" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> describes different statistics of the models’ output.
On deeper inspection, we observed that <span id="S4.SS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Video-LLaVA</span> often reformulates the prompt to a question (e.g., "What is the content of the video?").
<span id="S4.SS1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">PG-Video-LLaVA</span> implies more problems, producing a mix of unrelated, related questions, summaries, or empty strings.
<span id="S4.SS1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Video-LLaMA</span> never returns an empty string but sometimes fails to generate a question.
In contrast, the <span id="S4.SS1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Mistral-7B</span> generates more content-related questions.
When asked for more questions, all models tend to repeat themselves.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For <span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Rouge</span> and <span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">BertScore</span> on the VLM side, <span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Video-LLaVA</span> has the highest scores.
Since <span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Video-LLaVA</span> only generates short questions, the score automatically increases without providing proper context, as fewer words need to be compared.
The scores of <span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">PG-Video-LLaVA</span> are the worst since many empty outputs are generated.
Overall, the metrics do not reflect how well the questions match the video content since the question may differ from the ground truth, resulting in a lower score.
This is also visible in the values of <span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Mistral-7B</span>, which are not very high despite more content-related generation.
Considering the <span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">ICD</span> scores, their values are always positive.
This indicates that, on average, the output is more similar to the used video than to others of the same class.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2 </span>Fine-Tuning Setting</h3>

<section id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Training approach:</h5>

<div id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We fine-tuned <span id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">PG-Video-LLaVA</span> and <span id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Video-LLaMA</span> on the modified training data of <span id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">LearningQ</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite> to analyze whether these models can be optimized for multimodal question generation.
We used the models’ code provided by the authors, changed the batch size to two to account for computing capacity limitations, and adjusted the learning rate using the linear scaling rule <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>]</cite>.
We use the <span id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">13B</span> versions for both models.
Models are trained on the first prompt (see Section <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 Zero-Shot Setting ‣ 4 Comparing VLMs for Video Question Generation ‣ Enhancing the Learning Experience: Using Vision-Language Models to Generate Questions for Educational Videos" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>) since it is formulated in a more general way.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Results:</h5>

<div id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We still used all three prompts to ensure a better comparison with the zero-shot approach.
The first and second entries of Table <a href="#S4.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ Results: ‣ 4.2 Fine-Tuning Setting ‣ 4 Comparing VLMs for Video Question Generation ‣ Enhancing the Learning Experience: Using Vision-Language Models to Generate Questions for Educational Videos" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> describe the
fine-tuned models.
Compared to zero-shot, the number of generated questions increased.
However, <span id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">PG-Video-LLaVA</span> still struggles with Khan Academy videos, likely due to varied handwriting.
This leads to misinterpretations, and combined with transcripts, the model may produce unclear output.
<span id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Video-LLaMA</span> shows increased stability in generating questions, indicating a more robust adaptation to the task, even with different prompts.
The metrics <span id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">ROUGE</span>, <span id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">BERTScore</span> and <span id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">ICD</span> mostly improved.
Training on educational videos likely contributed to a better alignment with the task.
Even if no question is generated (see <span id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">PG-Video-LLaVA</span>), the output may be closer to the content, which can lead to improved scores.
This implies manual question analysis is still required for evaluating details like complexity and relevance, and to compare with the baselines.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T5" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5: </span>Evaluation of fine-tuned <span id="S4.T5.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">PG-Video-LLaVA</span> and <span id="S4.T5.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Video-LLaMA</span> across modalities (multi-modal, visual only [V], audio only [A]). <em id="S4.T5.11" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Quest.</em>, <span id="S4.T5.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Statem.</span>, and <span id="S4.T5.13" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Empty</span> denote the percentage of generated questions, statements, and empty outputs, respectively. Besides, the scores of the metrics <span id="S4.T5.14" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Rouge</span>, <span id="S4.T5.15" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">BertScore</span> and our metric (ICD) are given.</figcaption>
