</section>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.3 </span>Ablation Study</h3>

<div id="S4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given the multimodal nature of videos, it is unclear how important each modality is.
To gain a better insight, we evaluate the fine-tuned models with only one modality: replacing frames with black frames in one experiment and removing the audio track in another (second part of Table <a href="#S4.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ Results: ‣ 4.2 Fine-Tuning Setting ‣ 4 Comparing VLMs for Video Question Generation ‣ Enhancing the Learning Experience: Using Vision-Language Models to Generate Questions for Educational Videos" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">PG-Video-LLaVA</span> mostly generates questions using only frames or transcripts.
The outputs revealed that the model hallucinates when lacking one modality, generating more non-content-specific questions.
In contrast, <span id="S4.SS3.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Video-LLaMA</span> generates
fewer questions when using only frames, likely due to
handwriting quality in Khan Academy videos, while the audio-only approach performs similarly to the multimodal method.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Focusing on the metrics, the results for the <span id="S4.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">PG-Video-LLaVA</span> overall improve, likely due to more generated short questions, since they are more similar to the ground-truth questions structure, e.g., using the same question word.
Still, the <span id="S4.SS3.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">ICD</span> value of the audio-only approach is getting worse, given the impression that there is hardly any similarity to the content.
For <span id="S4.SS3.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Video-LLaMA</span>, almost all metric values are worse, which is caused by the fewer content-specific questions.
For a more detailed analysis, datasets with more diverse video presentation styles are required to clarify each modality’s significance within each style.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.4 </span>Evaluation of Question Structure</h3>

<figure id="S4.T6" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 6: </span>Distribution of question words (%) of <span id="S4.T6.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Mistral-7B</span> (M-7B), <span id="S4.T6.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Video-LLaVA</span> (V-L), <span id="S4.T6.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">PG-Video-LLaVA</span> (P-V-L) and <span id="S4.T6.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Video-LLaMA</span> (V-LM) on generated questions across approaches (GT: ground truth. *: fine-tuned; <span id="S4.T6.13" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">V</span>: frames only; <span id="S4.T6.14" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">A</span>: audio only). <span id="S4.T6.15" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">None</span> defines questions without a question word.</figcaption>
<table id="S4.T6.16" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="S4.T6.16.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T6.16.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T6.16.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Model</span></td>
<td id="S4.T6.16.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T6.16.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Where</span></td>
<td id="S4.T6.16.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T6.16.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Who</span></td>
<td id="S4.T6.16.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T6.16.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">When</span></td>
<td id="S4.T6.16.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T6.16.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">What</span></td>
<td id="S4.T6.16.1.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T6.16.1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Why</span></td>
