<section id="S4.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.5 </span>Qualitative Evaluation</h3>

<div id="S4.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Since most automatic evaluation metrics rely on ground-truth questions, they may not accurately assess whether a generated question is meaningful if it differs.
To investigate this, we qualitatively evaluate questions from six videos (three TED-ED and three Khan Academy videos) across three dimensions:</p>
<ul id="S4.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Relevance:</span> Does the generated question refer to the video content?</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Answerability:</span> Can the question be answered based on the video content?</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Levels of understanding:</span> Does the generated question require a certain level of understanding from the learner w.r.t. Bloom’s taxonomy?</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="S4.SS5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Relevance and answerability (binary values) are used to investigate if a generated question is meaningful and grounded in the video content similar to Elkins et al. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite>.
Bloom’s taxonomy <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>]</cite> was chosen for levels of understanding, as in <span id="S4.SS5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">LearningQ</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite> and related research <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>, <a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>, <a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">45</a>]</cite>.
For each approach (zero-shot and fine-tuned), two of the authors independently evaluated the first generated response from each prompt, followed by a discussion.
Additionally, Krippendorff’s alpha is calculated to assess the inter-rater reliability before discussion.
A total of <math id="S4.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="180" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>180</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">180</annotation></semantics></math> outputs is analyzed, with results and code available online<span id="footnote1" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">1</span>
              
              
              
            <a href="https://github.com/markossta/aied_2025_video_qg" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/markossta/aied_2025_video_qg</a></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Krippendorff’s alpha scores indicate moderate to good agreement for relevance and answerability (<math id="S4.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.71" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.71</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.71</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.79" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.79</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.79</annotation></semantics></math>).
In contrast, levels of understanding have a low agreement (<math id="S4.SS5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.43" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.43</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.43</annotation></semantics></math>), reflecting the complexity of evaluating levels of understanding.
This confirms inconsistencies, indicating the need for a more collaborative approach.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T8" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 8: </span>Results of manual evaluation (%) for <span id="S4.T8.17" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Mistral-7B</span> (M-7B), <span id="S4.T8.18" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Video-LLaVA</span> (V-L), <span id="S4.T8.19" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">PG-Video-LLaVA</span> (P-V-L) and <span id="S4.T8.20" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Video-LLaMA</span> (V-LM) across approaches (*: fine-tuned; <span id="S4.T8.21" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">V</span>: frames only; <span id="S4.T8.22" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">A</span>: audio only). The evaluation metrics are defined as <span id="S4.T8.23" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Rel.</span>: relevance, <span id="S4.T8.24" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Ans.</span>: answerability. and understanding levels: <span id="S4.T8.25" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">non</span> (no level), <span id="S4.T8.26" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">rem.</span> (remember), <span id="S4.T8.27" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">underst.</span> (understand), <span id="S4.T8.28" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">apply</span>, <span id="S4.T8.29" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">analyze</span>, <span id="S4.T8.30" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">eval.</span> (evaluate) and <span id="S4.T8.31" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">create</span>.
</figcaption>
